plan.md
workstreams/
insights.md
cold-clone-checklist.md
demo-script.md

# Logos module-builder Nix outputs (per-flake)
swap-module/result
swap-module/result-*
swap-module/.direnv
swap-module/generated_code/
swap-ui/result
swap-ui/result-*

# Legacy two-Basecamp instance dirs from the pre-scaffold flow
# (the `make basecamp-init-{maker,taker}` targets no longer exist; kept as a
# safety ignore for older working copies)
.basecamp/
swap-ui/.direnv
# swap-ui/flake.lock is deliberately NOT ignored (it was, until issue #60).
# Unpinned, swap-ui re-resolved logos-module-builder and the whole packaging
# stack from their branch HEADs on every single build, so two builds of the same
# commit could — and did — ship different bytes: regenerating the lock three days
# after the 0.3.0 release moved 14 nodes, including logos-module-builder itself.
# That is also the only reason swap_ui 0.3.0's manifest came out correct while
# swap 0.3.0's did not: swap_ui floated onto the display_name fix by luck, not by
# intent. Luck is not a release process, and it cuts the other way just as easily
# now that three variant legs on three runners merge into one .lgx.

# Logos dev-boost / agent context generated locally; not part of source
.agents/
.opencode/
.mcp.json
.sisyphus/
AGENTS.md

